Z||000000||Dumba$$||12-31-2001||10:58 AM||||engine wise i mean,<P>mine was just rebuilt 2500 miles ago <BR>i have :<BR>heads milled .020, ported exhaust, no cat,<BR>platinum +4's, msd coil,k&n, adj. fuel pressure reg., optima bat., polly dog bone,<BR>auto w/ shift kit,<BR> tomorrow it will become a 4.10 4spd. and polly cradle mt. bushings.<P>im sure i have more done to it but im having the usual brain fart  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><BR>other little --REASONABLE-- things i want to do:<BR>cold air intake, from DXR DAD,<BR>bored out tb,<BR>power pully,<BR>lower it<P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE <BR>98 acura cl 3.0<P>ever notice that people that own a fiero, either have, or have had other fieros?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||12-31-2001||11:41 AM||||Well you asked for it so here comes the long list.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>1. engine bored and stroked to 3.2 <BR>2. Custom Ross forged pistons @ 10:1 comp.<BR>3. stainless swirl polished valves<BR>4. Comp. Cams performance cam<BR>5. Comp. Cams. roller tipped rockers<BR>6. ported lower intake<BR>7. bored out t-body and upper plenum<BR>8. sprint headers (soon to be FOCOA headers)<BR>9. Ocelot performance exhaust (soon to be Borla)<BR>10.Hypertech adj. fuel pressure reg.<BR>11. ADS strip chip<BR>12. ADS super injectors. (soon to be Accel nineteen LBers)<BR>13. cat replaced with straight pipe<BR>14. Holley scoop with K&N filter<BR>15. lightweight racing wheels only weigh 13 LB's. also a lot of other weight has been cut<BR>16. ASP power pulley<P>I'm not finished with her yet and you can see most of the stuff that i've got planned to do to her this winter/spring but i'm also working on: getting the a new set of heads ported, more weight cut, and the trans worked out. I'm not sur eif i'll finish the trans and heads by this spring or if they will carry on into the summer.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>Activities Director<BR>Northern IL. Fiero Enthusiasts<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000002||LoW_KeY||12-31-2001||01:36 PM||||Here's what I got planned  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> and its only 3 months away hehe<P>All going to get done on a 3.4<P>1. 1.6 Cam<BR>2. 10:1 Ross pistons<BR>3. Bored .030 over<BR>4. Port/Polish<BR>5. Lifters<BR>6. Balanced/Blue printed<BR>7. Plenum powder coated speckled black<BR>8. 19/24 lb injectors<P>Things done.<P>1. Air Intake (I owe ya Craig *Fieromaster*)<BR>2. Under pulley<BR>3. Puter chip<BR>4. Bored TB/Plenum (still waiting to put plenum on)<P>That pretty much covers her.. hopefully I'll be happy with it.<P>-KC<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/low_keysig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierokid87||12-31-2001||02:26 PM||||Bored .30 over<BR>block decked .10<BR>heads milled .20<BR>3 angle valve grind<BR>SI Stainless steel performance valves<BR>MSD GM style coil<BR>MSD 6A Box<BR>Poly engien mount from Darel Morse<BR>Poly dog bone from Darel Morse<BR>lower drive line strut from Darel Morse<BR>Hyperutectic 9.5:1 pistons<BR>internally balanced crank<BR>rods matched to the lightest one<BR>Crane Compu Cam 2030 grind<BR>crane valve springs<BR>Rodney Dickmans vacume lines<BR>Ported TB, and Plenum<BR>Borla Exaust<BR>Free flow cat<BR>ported exaust manifolds<P>and some other things that I cant think of<P>Scott<BR><P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"> Fierokid's  Web site:</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="white">http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</FONT><P><FONT COLOR="blue">AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokid.gif"> ||||reg||1
